      "message": "[error] Line 393: 🔴 Removing `contact_metadata` from `DeviceSync` breaks mixed-version device sync: older clients still send incremental metadata updates in that field, and this version will silently drop them. That can cause permanent metadata divergence until some unrelated full-contact update happens. Keep backward-compatible decoding (e.g., retain an optional `contact_metadata` field for deserialization) and merge it in `AccountManager::onSyncData` as a fallback when present.",
